{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483821-d-tr-some-questions-about-scar-free-variations-the-conspiracies-have","id":1483821,"title":"[D:TR] Some questions about scar-free Variations the Conspiracies have","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-12T15:54:42-07:00","id":1483821,"title":"[D:TR] Some questions about scar-free Variations the Conspiracies have","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> This is my second question on Deviant: The Renegades, now with Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> I have questions about how to implement and how it works the scar-free Variations the Conspiracies can have as Icons. I have two question related to this subject:<br /> <br /> First, I want confirmation on what are the capacity of Icons to create scar-free Variations.<br /> <br /> This are the ones I found on the book:<ul><li>Give Magnitude 2 variation to all members of a Node and Magnitude 3 to the chief of the Node. [Pg. 222]</li> <li>Give 7 Magnitudes to spread on a group of agents, only one Variation per agent. So you can have a duo of Magnitude 5 guy and Magnitude 2 sidekick, seven Magnitude 1 squad and so on. [Pg. 258]</li> <li>Give Magnitude 3 variation related to a category (&quot;enchanced senses&quot; for example) to all members of the Conspiracy, all members of the Conspiracy have the same Variation but it can be changed with a Complexity 1 Project. [Pg. 259] This is the one make me question this because seems more useful and powerful than the Variation to a Node first option.</li> </ul>My second question is how the members activate this. I know in most examples this is like a Supernatural Power implanted on the member and so follow the rules for scar-free Variations on the Deviants: You choose attribute and if Controlled or Persistent.<br /> <br /> But for example for create Icons on the page 226 present this can be put on weapons and tools, something that also seems obvious certain types of Conspiracies would do. How they work in this case? The weapon that shoots lasers still using the lowest of the Strenght/Intelligence/Presence or the Magnitude of the wielder? Seems a bit off, but there is not more deepth explanation of Conspiracies being able to wield scar-free Variations.<br /> <br /> Thanks for you time and your answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T18:17:28-07:00","id":1483830,"title":"","content":"Reference the notes in Sacred Flesh for notes on how Scar-free Variations on non-Deviants are handled as a reference point. Note that several Variations, including Lash, are built to provide a solid basic effect with the first dot of Magnitude. If it's not a Directed Variation, you can sensibly treat it as Persistent unless it's an effect from a Variation with the Perpetual keyword that the conspiracy's users narratively have to turn on. Effects that use Scar Power use the user's Scar Power as normal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand what the first question is; yes, you have correctly identified the corebook's examples of Icons providing Scar-free Variations to a conspiracy, though you have misidentified the effect of the Vigilance Society's Sensory Augmentation Tank, which benefits agents of the Node it is attached to just like the sample Mnemonic Therapy Chamber does. Conspiracy Icons granting Scar-free Variations is, among other things, the sort of outcome many conspiracies are building toward on a larger scale (the Remade being imperfect stepping stones toward getting just the powers), and the fact that their availability is dependent upon the Icon is one reason to try and subvert a Node as well as a solid mechanical example of how organizations with supernatural involvement can bend the normal rules for supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T18:54:09-07:00","id":1483832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483821-d-tr-some-questions-about-scar-free-variations-the-conspiracies-have?p=1483830#post1483830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reference the notes in Sacred Flesh for notes on how Scar-free Variations on non-Deviants are handled as a reference point. Note that several Variations, including Lash, are built to provide a solid basic effect with the first dot of Magnitude. If it's not a Directed Variation, you can sensibly treat it as Persistent unless it's an effect from a Variation with the Perpetual keyword that the conspiracy's users narratively have to turn on. Effects that use Scar Power use the user's Scar Power as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question in this is: Then, if a Conspiracy creates a weapon with a Lash attack with Deadly that assumes a Physical Scar, then the damage of the weapon is the lower of the Strength or the Magnitude of the Lash? That is were I don't see the &quot;sense&quot; because a pistol don't do more <i>direct</i> damage because one Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483821-d-tr-some-questions-about-scar-free-variations-the-conspiracies-have?p=1483830#post1483830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand what the first question is; yes, you have correctly identified the corebook's examples of Icons providing Scar-free Variations to a conspiracy, though you have misidentified the effect of the Vigilance Society's Sensory Augmentation Tank, which benefits agents of the Node it is attached to just like the sample Mnemonic Therapy Chamber does. Conspiracy Icons granting Scar-free Variations is, among other things, the sort of outcome many conspiracies are building toward on a larger scale (the Remade being imperfect stepping stones toward getting just the powers), and the fact that their availability is dependent upon the Icon is one reason to try and subvert a Node as well as a solid mechanical example of how organizations with supernatural involvement can bend the normal rules for supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more about me wanting to understand what is the &quot;intended balance&quot;, why the Vigilance Society's Sensory Augmentation Tank gives Magnitude 3 Variations to the members of the entire Node but the Mnemonic Therapy Chamber gives Magnitude 2 to the members and only 3 to the chief?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T19:23:43-07:00","id":1483834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483821-d-tr-some-questions-about-scar-free-variations-the-conspiracies-have?p=1483832#post1483832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My question in this is: Then, if a Conspiracy creates a weapon with a Lash attack with Deadly that assumes a Physical Scar, then the damage of the weapon is the lower of the Strength or the Magnitude of the Lash? That is were I don't see the &quot;sense&quot; because a pistol don't do more <i>direct</i> damage because one Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few different ways you could handle this scenario:<br /> <br /> 1. In your specific case of a physical Deadly Lash, the weapon keys off the user's Strength to calculate damage because it's a weird hypertechnological/supernatural/etc effect that defies modern understanding of the world. Maybe you have to plug the pistol into your body and it taps into your natural biorhythms to fuel its laser blasts, or whatnot.<br /> <br /> 2. In places where player-facing calculations don't make sense, choose a different parameter or a set value (maybe a Deadly Lash pistol is keyed to Dexterity instead, or they're engineered to always have a damage rating of 3). The specific rules for Variations and Scars are more for the sake of players and making sure everyone is on the same page, while a similar effect for a Storyteller-controlled Conspiracy doesn't need that same level of granularity so long as you're consistent, especially as I get the feeling that some of these relevant Icons aren't Variations per se but rather special effects that are best modeled using the tools at hand.<br /> <br /> 3. Don't choose mechanical effects that clash with the fictive elements in play. If Deadly doesn't work for the concept your Icon is going for, consider a different perk like Blasting.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that the Devoted Companion will go a bit more in-depth, when it comes out, into how to design Icons for Conspiracies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T20:23:52-07:00","id":1483840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483821-d-tr-some-questions-about-scar-free-variations-the-conspiracies-have?p=1483832#post1483832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is were I don't see the &quot;sense&quot; because a pistol don't do more <i>direct</i> damage because one Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is a situation where it makes zero sense to use Lash to model a pistol instead of just\u2026 giving your goons pistols. A Cutting Firearms Lash with Deadly and Gunshot will have a Damage rating of at least 2 in the hands of all but the weakest/dumbest/least charismatic of wielders, and a Devastating Insidious Lash will be stronger than that at the price of contenting with Resistance. These are powers being put in the hands of Storyteller characters who are part of an organized group \u2014 management can afford the negligible vetting to figure out if it's worth sending somebody who can't lift a sack of flour to use the Strong Bullets Gun to bring in a transformed fugitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is more about me wanting to understand what is the &quot;intended balance&quot;, why the Vigilance Society's Sensory Augmentation Tank gives Magnitude 3 Variations to the members of the entire Node but the Mnemonic Therapy Chamber gives Magnitude 2 to the members and only 3 to the chief? </div> </div> </div>Probably because the Sensory Augmentation Tank is an Icon from a Standing 7 conspiracy connected enough to have lost a nuclear weapon and because the Variations that fit its criteria include at least one that doesn't <i>qualify</i> until Magnitude 3 (and a different one that can be purchased multiple times and only has Magnitude above 1 in one case).<br /> <br /> The Mnemonic Therapy Chamber exists to provide the listed benefit to its Node, presumably isn't attached to a conspiracy with global reach, and involves a Variation whose main long-term benefit comes at the first dot; it can manage providing a slightly &quot;weaker&quot; effect than the fine-tuned procedures of a shadow government that needs to cover &quot;this process is why the Vigilance Society's agents can smell the Divergence or see through walls, as expected from a conspiracy whose Divergence program specialized in those powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> As espritdecalmar observes, more granular balance notes on Icon design can probably be expected in the supplement about characters who work for the conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}